LittleWhiteMouse, Chaotic Male Human Priest  (on NAO)
(Ascended Female)

This was my first serious attempt on NAO, and I had fun with it!
I managed to pull off a MR-less, wishless Ascention.

This is kinda long, BTW, and bit scattered at points.

I found a very early BoHolding.

Sokoban was also early (level 6?  branch on lvl 4)
Had "oReflection - woot!

I had two pet fs in mines, which I did next...
But no Magic Whistle for a long time.  This makes it rather
irritating to keep pets around, let me tell you!

Farmed a few brown puddings for a little bit to get Poison Resistance.
Picked up Electric on the way, but never got Cold.  Go figure.  Dug out
fair bit of Oracle level while waiting for satiation to end.

Remember how everyone always says, Try on Every piece of armor?  Well...
I found lots of +4, +5 equip - +5 Hard Shoes, +5 Gloves !
Some very nice cloak - lost it due to a Polymorph Trap.
Another nice cloak - lost it due to a Polymorph Trap.
I finally kept a +3 Dwarvish one.

Eventually polied Dumb Cat (she was slow on stairs) into a Silver D.
  (woot!)

I tried to get an artifact weapon...all I got was Sting.  And Orcrist.

Gee...thanks.  I used a +5 hammer!  I kept this through most of the 
game, only ditching it for Astral because it was heavy.

I had to do the quest w/o a magic whistle.  And I like pets :-(

At one point, an egg in my bag hatched, and I was "daddy" to a 
cave spider w/ something like 4 hp.  I put an my =oConflict and let
Dumb Cat squish it.

Got Dumb Cat up to a high level (many wraiths).  Came down to Castle
and discovered Big Purple L...who prompty attacked and cursed half my
stuff...  But between me and Another Cat, we took care of it, and I had 
a blessed ?oRemoveCurse to take care of the problem!

Did Castle - played w/ drawbridge a fair bit - got rid of Rs and another L.

Found Vorpal Blade in storeroom of Castle (used boulders to get past
half the trapdoors)  And some speed boots.

But I lost Dumb Cat, the Silver D, somehow...  I checked the whole dungeon,
but never found it...  Oh well.  I even went down to the VotD...and had to
come back across 2 trapdoors w/o Levitation (oops).

About this time, I decided to go without MR - I'd been playing around
with the idea for a while, and this just happened to be the time.  I
also decided to forgo the Castle Wand and go wishless.  (I did tote it 
around w/ me to Astral - no sense keeping Wishless and dying, now is there?)

I picked up Another Cat, was keeping it around , and then
managed to get Stormy...So I prompty slaughtered Another Cat....twice.
About this time, I found a Magic Whistle!

Decided to polypile - wanted to try for some MMs, since I was
going wishless...kinda defeats the point...but oh well.

Went over to Fort Ludos, cleaned it out, took cash to MineTown, slaughtered
everyone there but the Priest (and Izchak, of course).  I left priest alive
so nothing would eat my cash :-)

Came back to the fort and polypiled.  Got some useful rings, but no
"oLS...  Also got some missing scrolls (Genocide and Charging).  At
this point, I had ID as a spell (a lot of spells this game, and I 
didn't even polypile +)

Eventually decided to poly to Xorn to eat rings:  needed Poly Control.
So I got it, and also got Magical Breathing (woot!)  Also an oilskin 
bag.  That's handy.  But no TeleControl.

Then decided I wanted some SDSM.  So I polied to a Gray Dragon, realized
I was male...and then tried polying into a human, hoping to change sex.
By the time I had lost 3 levels (down to 12), I decided to go with the
"oChanging I had...  So I polied back into a Gray Dragon, and proceeded
to turn Fort Ludos Gardens into a big field of my eggs.  After I had about
20 Gray Dragons, it finally dawned on me that Gray Dragons give GDSM,
not SDSM...  So I put on my =oConflict, and let my kids slaughter one
another.  I killed the last 4 w/ +7 Stormy while they were eating their
brothers and sisters.  I tried again w/ Silver DRagons, and got 13 live
pets.  I slowly leveled them up and slaughtered them as soon as they
became Silver Dragons.  (My brothers words:  Way to encourge Slack!)
I was down to 6 by the time I got my SDSM...  I left two of them behind
(6 and 11, I think), and I took 2, 7, 8 and 9 with me.

Genociding stuff:
L
;
h  (on principle)
Golden Naga

In the VotD:
 9 bites 7.  9 hits 7.  9 misses 7.  8 bites 7.  8 hits 7.  8 hits 7.  7 misses 8.  7 hits 8.

I wonder if I can get "7 eats 9"... Alas, 7 seems to have been raised Feral...and I lost 8, too...
But 9 still has a saddle.

After this, I took a long vacation, and when I came back, I had to re-remember where
all of it is...always exciting.

Back to the VotD, found a Black D, ate it, felt very Firm. Ok, good.
Maybe I should have tamed it - could have been useful with =oConflict 
and Reflection...next time.

Learned Charm Monster - I now have 27 spells memorized :-)  
Thanks to a +5 robe, I can even cast them!

I now have 3 silver Ds, 2 black Ds, and a J.  Vlad was a wimp.

Magic Mapping made Gehennom easy!  Orcus was a bit exciting, 
tho - when my head ached, it *ached*.  I went from 345 hp to 
around 150...  Ouch!

Found another MM in Gehennom - means I managed to reverse 
genocide enuf Tengu to get TC.

Finally realized I can alchemize to get hallucination, so I felt braver :-)
(if you're hallucinating, Touch of Death won't kill you...unless it's Death)
I also got 500 hp thanks to Alchemy!

For my ascention run, I wore the single "oLS I had.  Thankfully, never needed it.
I had a bunch of pet J and Silver and Black D.  We made short work of most stuff...
Rodney went down to Orcus' /oDeath before he could do anything exciting, so I 
grabbed the book, collected my herd, and went off to the VS.

The Sanctum was my first experience with enemy Priests...  The extra hp helped - 
those spells hurt w/o MR!  I got the High Priest w/ a !oParalysis, and then hacked
him to bits.  Took a sec to kick Moloch's altar on the way out.  Summoned my pets,
a raised up, thru the ceiling!

The run was actually pretty easy.  Never saw Rodney.  Got tossed back maybe twice.
I had the spell Remove Curse, so that was never a problem.  I rode Silver D 3 thru
the dungeon after 9 croaked somewhere.

Earth was **really** exciting!  I drank a !oHallucination before going up there...
What a trip!  I had 6 or 7 pets, and all of the sudden, I'm fighting someone I 
can't see!  Someone who just blew away my +5 robe (!!!)  I think I killed 3 of
my own pets with Stormy, but I got Rodney by the end of it - only had one "out 
of body experience" and that was enuf thank you!

I poked around for some replacement cloak, but eventually went on.  Not bringing
an extra was kinda dumb - I couldn't cast my offensive spells anymore...

Anyway, Earth was no problem after that.  Air was a bit more exciting - I tamed
several E.  I even had a few left when I got to the portal.  But they didn't last
2 minutes on Fire...  3 died from underneath me, and from then on, I was on foot.
I tried raising them, but they'd had enough of me, and I had to let Stormy suck
their souls.  After that, it was merely "run away from the Es"

Water was silly - there were Gremlins.  And I lost most of my critters.  I made 
it out with a Fire Elemental and a Minotaur.

Astral...very very difficult.  I had 6 !oFH, and I used them all.  I tried left
first (Famine), but that was a bust.  Tamed a purple Worm, tho - that was good.
It was also my last scroll of taming.  I think I wrote that one while I was 
inside his belly.  I also managed to anger the high priest...who took me down
to half my hp in two moves.  And confused me.  Extra Speed and !oFH got me out
of there alive.  I also picked up a new Robe - not that I had the Power to use it.

The middle Altar had Death, but he was too close to the door for me to just pass
by him.  So I blasted him with wands, and then took him out with some +7 daggers.
But middle wasn't mine either.  <grr>

So I had to go past Death *again*.  About this time, I was wishing I had taken
along a /oLocking (DOH - just realized I probably knew Wizard Lock).  Anyway, I'd
kicked in the doors, so Death followed me into the corridor, and I had to kill
him again.  Not fun, let me tell you!

But I managed.  Then, **just** before I met Pestilence, I got burdoned by taking
!oParalysis out of my BoH.  **DOH**.  I went thru my last !oFH there, got back
to unburdoned, let Pestilance have it with the Paralysis-Juice, and ran for the
door!  2 A and a few @ behind me, but I knew it was my altar.  Careful not to
anger any priests, I went to the Altar, double-checked everything, called in my
purple worm (only pet left alive), and Ascended!

Major difficulties:
Hit Points.
Pets + Hallucination.
Scared to death of Death.

Major advantages:
Stormy + slaughtering pets is fuuuun for a chaotic!

                                                                                         
                                                                                         
                                                                                         
